{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.ThurstonVolumeAdditivity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.ThurstonVolumeAdditivity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Complex.Log","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.UnitInterval","lean:module:QOU.Knot.FlatTetrahedra"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.thurstonVolumeAdditivity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.thurstonVolumeAdditivity","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/thurston-volume-additivity.lean#L107-L120","doc":"**Thurston volume additivity** (conditional theorem, §3b-cond).\nGiven an instance of `HasThurstonTriangulation M hypVol`, every\npoint of `M` admits an ideal triangulation whose shape-parameter\nBloch–Wigner sum equals the hyperbolic volume.\n\nThe proof body has no `sorry`; the only unproved input is the\nclass instance, which is the classical [thurston1978] theorem. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:thurston-volume-additivity","label":"prop:thurston-volume-additivity","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/thurston-volume-additivity.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.HasThurstonTriangulation.volume_eq_thurston","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.HasThurstonTriangulation.volume_eq_thurston","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/thurston-volume-additivity.lean#L104-L104","doc":"The volume coincides with the Thurston sum of Bloch–Wigner\nvalues on the chosen triangulation.\nRef: [thurston1978] http://library.msri.org/books/gt3m/ ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.HasThurstonTriangulation.triangulation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.HasThurstonTriangulation.triangulation","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/thurston-volume-additivity.lean#L100-L100","doc":"Per-point ideal triangulation realising the hyperbolic volume. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.HasThurstonTriangulation.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.HasThurstonTriangulation.mk","kind":"ctor","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/thurston-volume-additivity.lean#L97-L97","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.HasThurstonTriangulation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.HasThurstonTriangulation","kind":"class","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/thurston-volume-additivity.lean#L89-L105","doc":"Class-axiomatisation of Thurston's existence theorem\n(AGENTS.md §3b-cond): for every hyperbolic 3-manifold `M`\nequipped with a hyperbolic-volume function `hypVol`, an ideal\ntriangulation realising the volume exists.\n\nThe single field `triangulation_exists` is the classical\n[thurston1978] result; an instance is the conjectural input\nthat downstream conditional theorems consume. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.thurstonVolume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.thurstonVolume","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/thurston-volume-additivity.lean#L84-L87","doc":"Hyperbolic volume computed from an ideal triangulation as the\nsum of Bloch-Wigner dilogarithms over its shape parameters. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.IdealTriangulation.shape_nontrivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.IdealTriangulation.shape_nontrivial","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/thurston-volume-additivity.lean#L82-L82","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.IdealTriangulation.shapes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.IdealTriangulation.shapes","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/thurston-volume-additivity.lean#L81-L81","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.IdealTriangulation.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.IdealTriangulation.mk","kind":"ctor","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/thurston-volume-additivity.lean#L80-L80","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.IdealTriangulation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.IdealTriangulation","kind":"structure","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/thurston-volume-additivity.lean#L78-L82","doc":"Data of a Thurston ideal triangulation: a finite list of shape\nparameters zᵢ ∈ ℂ ∖ {0, 1}. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.blochWigner_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.blochWigner_real","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/thurston-volume-additivity.lean#L66-L76","doc":"**Bloch-Wigner vanishes on the real line — now a theorem.**\n\nDischarges the former `axiom blochWigner_real`.  Holds for every\nreal `x` with no hypotheses at all, including the junk-value cases\n`x = 0` and `x = 1`, where Lean's `1/0 = 0` still lands on `arg = 0`.\n\nThis is the statement the block's prose uses to conclude that torus\nknots — whose shape parameters are all real — have zero volume. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.blochWigner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.blochWigner","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/thurston-volume-additivity.lean#L57-L64","doc":"The Bloch-Wigner dilogarithm `D : ℂ → ℝ`.\n\n**No longer an axiom.**  This is the corpus's real Bloch–Wigner,\n`QOU.Archimedean.BlochWigner_lob = Λ(θ₁)+Λ(θ₂)+Λ(θ₃)`, which\n`QOU/Knot/KummerRadial.lean` proves equals\n`Im (Li₂ z) + log‖z‖ · arg(1−z)` on the upper half plane. ","signatureChunk":0}]}